"M12","site":"Newcastle Eldon Sq","region":"scotland","type":"Outlier vs estate","headline":"mean 6.0 against an estate average of 4.99","detail":"1.5 standard deviations above the group"},{"sev":"med","rank":2,"kind":"chicken","loc":"Maki Shoreditch","code":"M19","site":"Shoreditch","region":"south","type":"Outlier vs estate","headline":"mean 6.0 against an estate average of 4.99","detail":"1.5 standard deviations above the group"}],"resolution":{"whole_only":27,"lines":36,"pct":75.0,"note":"Most of the estate only ever records whole numbers. A refractometer reads to one decimal, so a whole number is a rounded number. On a window only 1.0 or 2.0 wide, rounding to the nearest whole unit is a big fraction of the tolerance and it hides small drifts entirely. Sites already reporting decimals prove the meters can do it."},"cases":[{"loc":"Maki O2 Arena","code":"MAF3","site":"O2 London","region":"franchise","kind":"pork","priority":"P1","when":"this week","headline":"Not measuring","response":"Unannounced visit. Watch the check being taken, then take it yourself on the same pot and compare. If the refractometer is missing, broken or uncalibrated, replace it before anything else. Do not treat this as a broth problem until a real reading exists.","evidence":"one DEC-witnessed reading, plus 5 consecutive days of varying readings after","owner":"Matt Polak (Executive Chef) (escalated from Matthew Jenner)","mean":6.0,"in_spec_pct":100.0,"under":0,"over":0,"missed":0,"flags":["Flatline"],"flag_count":1,"runs_open":5,"first_seen":"2026-09-20","escalated":true,"owner_original":"Matthew Jenner (BDM, via the franchisee)","escalation_note":"open for 5 consecutive runs, escalated to the Executive Chef"},{"loc":"Maki Manchester LTD","code":"M9","site":"Manchester","region":"midlands","kind":"chicken","priority":"P1","when":"this week","headline":"Consistently too strong","response":"Method check at the pass. Watch one batch made start to finish: what vessel is the water measured with, and is the ratio the current spec? Too strong almost always means under-watering a concentrate. Re-read with the chef present and agree the ratio in writing before you leave.","evidence":"7 consecutive readings inside 4.0 to 5.0","owner":"Matt Polak (Executive Chef) (escalated from Artur Mroczkowski)","mean":6.0,"in_spec_pct":0.0,"under":0,"over":1,"missed":0,"flags":["Out of spec","Outlier vs estate"],"flag_count":2,"runs_open":2,"first_seen":"2026-10-11","escalated":true,"owner_original":"Artur Mroczkowski (DEC North England & Midlands)","escalation_note":"open for 2 consecutive runs, escalated to the Executive Chef"},{"loc":"Maki Newcastle Ltd","code":"M12","site":"Newcastle Eldon Sq","region":"scotland","kind":"chicken","priority":"P1","when":"this week","headline":"Consistently too strong","response":"Method check at the pass. Watch one batch made start to finish: what vessel is the water measured with, and is the ratio the current spec? Too strong almost always means under-watering a concentrate. Re-read with the chef present and agree the ratio in writing before you leave.","evidence":"7 consecutive readings inside 4.0 to 5.0","owner":"Matt Polak (Executive Chef) (escalated from Penny)","mean":6.0,"in_spec_pct":0.0,"under":0,"over":1,"missed":0,"flags":["Out of spec","Outlier vs estate"],"flag_count":2,"runs_open":10,"first_seen":"2026-08-16","escalated":true,"owner_original":"Penny (DEC Scotland & Newcastle)","escalation_note":"open for 10 consecutive runs, escalated to the Executive Chef"},{"loc":"Maki Aberdeen Ltd","code":"M13","site":"Aberdeen","region":"scotland","kind":"chicken","priority":"P1","when":"this week","headline":"Consistently too strong","response":"Method check at the pass. Watch one batch made start to finish: what vessel is the water measured with, and is the ratio the current spec? Too strong almost always means under-watering a concentrate. Re-read with the chef present and agree the ratio in writing before you leave.","evidence":"7 c